        "id": 1881539
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-20T16:50:08Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "I don\u0027t see why this removes us the capacity to apply common configs to all modules in the future, could you clarify here ?\n\nAlso I think here we are falling into the YAGNI (You Aren\u0027t Going to Need It) principle. We are planning for something that we don\u0027t know if we will need it.",
      "parentUuid": "eb5312a1_d72572e2",
      "revId": "e755143142167f2707992b3aa777e703826a0fa1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1a538b43_a0d0c912",
        "filename": "system/build/Android.bp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 19,
      "author": {
        "id": 1964701
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-21T23:18:55Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "In the next step, it is quite clear that we are going to need to apply Int-San and possibly CFI (not clear whether it is enabled in other places or not).\n\nI think it is a better option to leave it like this, just be careful when adding \nnew stuff to it.\n\nWe can change the name from `fluoride` to `bluetooth`, but narrowing it to cflags is undesired.",
      "parentUuid": "a26b1e12_fee74828",
      "revId": "e755143142167f2707992b3aa777e703826a0fa1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bda98ed4_29b6fc15",
        "filename": "system/build/Android.bp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 19,
      "author": {
        "id": 1881539
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-21T23:31:03Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "\u003e In the next step, it is quite clear that we are going to need to apply Int-San and possibly CFI (not clear whether it is enabled in other places or not).\n\nI wasn\u0027t aware of that, however I would say that this should not go into `bluetooth_cflags` as this would apply to everything, test and tools included.\n\nIf I understand correctly we will want to do that to harden the production stack and so this should be applied to defaults used by the production code e.g: `fluoride_defaults` and `gd_defaults`.\n\n\u003e I think it is a better option to leave it like this, just be careful when adding new stuff to it.\n\nThe history of the stack showed us that this doesn\u0027t really work :/. `common_options` is too wide for me, maybe `_cflags` is too narrow, but I prefer for it to be too narrow and open it up later than the other way around.\n\nAlso for me this has the added benefit that when we will change it, with the name change we will understand the impact of it (has this update all the users) and review if it\u0027s indeed applicable to all this targets.",
      "parentUuid": "1a538b43_a0d0c912",
      "revId": "e755143142167f2707992b3aa777e703826a0fa1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7473fe6d_306067f5",
        "filename": "system/build/Android.bp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 19,
      "author": {
        "id": 1964701
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-21T23:47:06Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "If you insist on making the change, I don\u0027t mind, but just make sure we have a mechanism to apply common changes in build configs and document it properly.\n\nIdeally, as you mentioned, we should have option to config different types of code, e.g. code for (1) unit testing and fuzzing, (2) dogfooding, and (3) product build. I think the product variant in soong is intended for this purpose, if we use product variant properly, one such common defaults should be enough to address all types of code. \n\nIt is up to you to, whether to use one common defaults for all types of code, or use separate defaults for different types of code. Just make sure we have the mechanism to apply common change to a type of file.",
      "parentUuid": "bda98ed4_29b6fc15",
      "revId": "e755143142167f2707992b3aa777e703826a0fa1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d6aefa60_171ca2d4",
        "filename": "system/build/Android.bp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 19,
      "author": {
        "id": 1881539
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-22T01:33:37Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "\u003e If you insist on making the change\n\nYes I do :)\n\n\u003e I think the product variant in soong is intended for this purpose, if we use product variant properly, one such common defaults should be enough to address all types of code.\n\nNot really, for example you cannot target `fuzzing, (2) dogfooding, and (3) product build` explicitly. Also I think it\u0027s a bad idea to change the way we build bluetooth depending on the product variant, we should instead have one configuration per Soong target and if you want more you create other targets. \n\n\u003e It is up to you to, whether to use one common defaults for all types of code, or use separate defaults for different types of code. Just make sure we have the mechanism to apply common change to a type of file.\n\nAs you cannot really use one common default for all type of code, you are left with doing a tree of default and having \"cflags\" all common root for everything make sense to me.",
      "parentUuid": "7473fe6d_306067f5",
      "revId": "e755143142167f2707992b3aa777e703826a0fa1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
